ton is a material control defect even if other navigation is available. This does not apply to excluded advertisements or auxiliary external widgets. Distinguish the button itself from decorative animation around it.", "criteria": {"meets": "Core interface meets this dimension under the category contract and contextual materiality policy.", "material_defect": "An observable material defect in core information or essential controls violates this dimension after applying contextual exclusions.", "insufficient": "Evidence is genuinely insufficient to assess essential interface requirements, not simply different or missing an optional region."}}, "evidence_coherence": {"type": "choice", "instructions": "Assess whether the supplied states belong to the intended reference/target comparison under its category and form a coherent assessable set. A permissible dynamic, advertising or regenerated-layout difference is not incoherence. Evaluate localized content/presentation/control defects in their own dimensions rather than treating every such difference as a mismatched evidence set.", "criteria": {"meets": "Core interface meets this dimension under the category contract and contextual materiality policy.", "material_defect": "An observable material defect in core information or essential controls violates this dimension after applying contextual exclusions.", "insufficient": "Evidence is genuinely insufficient to assess essential interface requirements, not simply different or missing an optional region."}}, "semantic_adequacy": {"type": "choice", "instructions": "Do the core target text, imagery and labels convey coherent meaning for the page purpose under the contextual materiality policy? Optional unavailable media and temporal differences alone do not destroy that meaning.", "criteria": {"meets": "Core interface meets this dimension under the category contract and contextual materiality policy.", "material_defect": "An observable material defect in core information or es